IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — THE RATE OF TAX ON CHARGEABLE INCOME.
--
-- Who is resident (s 2); the rates (ss 42, 43, Second Schedule), the partial
-- and start-up exemptions for companies (s 43(6)-(6D), (10)-(13)), the flat
-- rates on non-residents' gross income (s 43(3)-(5)), the non-resident reliefs
-- (ss 40A-40D), the child rebate (s 42A), and the company remissions for
-- YA 2024 and YA 2025 (ss 92J, 92L).
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt.

§ `The rate of tax`

§§ `The period this encoding states the law for`

-- The text is consolidated as at 6 Oct 2026. Most provisions are stated by
-- year of assessment, and the earlier versions of many were replaced without
-- their old text being kept. The computation of tax is encoded for YA 2024
-- onwards (FORK I1); an earlier YA refuses. Tables the Act itself keeps for
-- earlier YAs (the Second Schedule) are encoded as printed.
@ref s 2 "year of assessment"; Legislative History
GIVEN ya IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law is encoded for YA` ya MEANS
    IF   ya LESS THAN 2024
    THEN REFUSE "the Act as it applied before the year of assessment 2024 is not encoded"
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `Residence (s 2)`

-- s 2 "resident in Singapore": "(a) in relation to an individual, means a person
-- who, in the year preceding the year of assessment, resides in Singapore except
-- for such temporary absences therefrom as may be reasonable and not
-- inconsistent with a claim by such person to be resident in Singapore, and
-- includes a person who is physically present or who exercises an employment
-- (other than as a director of a company) in Singapore for 183 days or more
-- during the year preceding the year of assessment; and (b) in relation to a
-- company or body of persons, means a company or body of persons the control
-- and management of whose business is exercised in Singapore". s 2(2): a part
-- of a day counts as a day.
@ref s 2 "resident in Singapore", s 2(2)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of person`
      r IS A `Residence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `resident in Singapore:` k `,` r IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` THEN
            r's `resides in Singapore, except reasonable temporary absences`
        OR  r's `days physically present in Singapore` AT LEAST 183
        OR  r's `days exercising an employment in Singapore, other than as a director` AT LEAST 183
    WHEN `a company`         THEN r's `control and management of the business exercised in Singapore`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN r's `control and management of the business exercised in Singapore`
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "s 2 defines residence only for individuals, companies and bodies of persons; for this person it is an input"

§§ `The Second Schedule — rates on an individual's chargeable income`

-- A band of a progressive table: the width of the band, and the rate on every
-- dollar in it. The last band of each table is open-ended.
DECLARE `Band` HAS
    `width` IS A NUMBER
    `rate`  IS A NUMBER

GIVEN bands IS A LIST OF `Band`
      income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax by bands` bands `on` income MEANS
    CONSIDER bands
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN b FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   null rest OR income AT MOST b's `width`
        THEN (IF income GREATER THAN 0 THEN income TIMES b's `rate` ELSE 0)
        ELSE b's `width` TIMES b's `rate` PLUS `the tax by bands` rest `on` (income MINUS b's `width`)

-- Second Schedule Part A, Table 1: YA 2012 (individual or Hindu joint family)
-- and YAs 2013-2016 (individual).
@ref Second Schedule Part A Table 1
GIVETH A LIST OF `Band`
`Table 1` MEANS
    --        width    rate
    LIST (`Band` OF 20000, 0),
         (`Band` OF 10000, 2%),
         (`Band` OF 10000, 3.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 7%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 11.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 15%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 17%),
         (`Band` OF 120000, 18%),
         (`Band` OF 0, 20%)

-- Table 2: YAs 2017-2023.
@ref Second Schedule Part A Table 2
GIVETH A LIST OF `Band`
`Table 2` MEANS
    LIST (`Band` OF 20000, 0),
         (`Band` OF 10000, 2%),
         (`Band` OF 10000, 3.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 7%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 11.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 15%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 18%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 19%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 19.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 20%),
         (`Band` OF 0, 22%)

-- Table 3: YA 2024 and subsequent YAs.
@ref Second Schedule Part A Table 3
GIVETH A LIST OF `Band`
`Table 3` MEANS
    LIST (`Band` OF 20000, 0),
         (`Band` OF 10000, 2%),
         (`Band` OF 10000, 3.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 7%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 11.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 15%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 18%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 19%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 19.5%),
         (`Band` OF 40000, 20%),
         (`Band` OF 180000, 22%),
         (`Band` OF 500000, 23%),
         (`Band` OF 0, 24%)

-- The open-ended last band has width 0 in the tables; `the tax by bands`
-- treats the last band as unlimited.
@ref s 42(1); Second Schedule Part A
GIVEN ya     IS A NUMBER
      income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the resident individual rates for YA` ya `on chargeable income of` income MEANS
    BRANCH IF ya LESS THAN 2012 THEN REFUSE "the Second Schedule does not print rates before the year of assessment 2012"
           IF ya AT MOST 2016   THEN `the tax by bands` `Table 1` `on` income
           IF ya AT MOST 2023   THEN `the tax by bands` `Table 2` `on` income
           OTHERWISE                 `the tax by bands` `Table 3` `on` income

§§ `Section 43 — companies, non-residents, trustees and executors`

-- s 43(1): "(a) every company or body of persons, tax at the rate of 17% ...;
-- (b) every individual not resident in Singapore — (i) for the year of
-- assessment 2023 or a preceding year of assessment, ... 22% ...; and (ii)
-- for the year of assessment 2024 and subsequent years of assessment, ...
-- 24% ...; and (c) every other person not resident in Singapore, trustee (other
-- than the trustee of an incapacitated person) and executor, ... 17%".
-- s 43(8): 17% reads 20% for YAs 2005-2007 and 18% for YAs 2008-2009.
@ref s 43(1), (8)
GIVEN ya IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the company rate for YA` ya MEANS
    BRANCH IF ya AT MOST 2004 THEN REFUSE "s 43(8) gives the rate only from the year of assessment 2005"
           IF ya AT MOST 2007 THEN 20%
           IF ya AT MOST 2009 THEN 18%
           OTHERWISE 17%

@ref s 43(1)(b)
GIVEN ya IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-resident individual rate for YA` ya MEANS
    IF ya AT MOST 2023 THEN 22% ELSE 24%

DECLARE `Basis of charge` IS ONE OF
    `the Second Schedule rates for a resident individual`   -- s 42(1)
    `a flat rate` HAS `rate` IS A NUMBER                    -- s 43(1)

-- s 42(1): the Second Schedule applies to "every person (other than a body of
-- persons, a company, a person not resident in Singapore, a trustee who is not
-- the trustee of an incapacitated person, or an executor)"; s 43(1) to the
-- rest. A Hindu joint family falls under s 42(1) if resident.
@ref ss 42(1), 43(1)
GIVEN ya         IS A NUMBER
      k          IS A `Kind of person`
      resident   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Basis of charge`
`the basis of charge for YA` ya `on` k `, resident:` resident MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a company`                 THEN `a flat rate` (`the company rate for YA` ya)                 -- (1)(a)
    WHEN `a body of persons`         THEN `a flat rate` (`the company rate for YA` ya)                 -- (1)(a)
    WHEN `a trustee of another trust` THEN `a flat rate` (`the company rate for YA` ya)                -- (1)(c)
    WHEN `an executor`               THEN `a flat rate` (`the company rate for YA` ya)                 -- (1)(c)
    WHEN `an individual` THEN
        IF resident THEN `the Second Schedule rates for a resident individual` ELSE `a flat rate` (`the non-resident individual rate for YA` ya)   -- (1)(b)
    OTHERWISE
        IF resident THEN `the Second Schedule rates for a resident individual` ELSE `a flat rate` (`the company rate for YA` ya)              -- (1)(c)

§§ `Partial and start-up exemptions for companies (s 43(6)-(6D), (10)-(13))`

-- The facts that make a company a "qualifying company" (s 43(10), (11)).
DECLARE `Start-up facts` HAS
    `incorporated in Singapore`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Singapore for the YA`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limited by guarantee`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of shareholders, directly and beneficially` IS A NUMBER
    `all shareholders (or members) individuals throughout the basis period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an individual held at least 10% throughout the basis period` IS A BOOLEAN   -- of issued ordinary shares, or of contributions on winding up
    `incorporated on or after 26 February 2013`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `undertakes property development, itself or as a partner` IS A BOOLEAN       -- s 43(11)(a)-(b), (12)
    `its only activity is holding investments, itself or through a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 43(11)(c)-(d)
    `YA of incorporation`                               IS A NUMBER  -- the YA whose basis period includes incorporation

-- s 43(10) "qualifying company"; s 43(11): one incorporated on or after
-- 26 February 2013 is not, if it undertakes property development or its only
-- activity is holding investments.
@ref s 43(10) "qualifying company", (11)
GIVEN f IS A `Start-up facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying company under s 43(10):` f IF
        f's `incorporated in Singapore`
    AND "(a)" ... f's `resident in Singapore for the YA`
    AND "(b)" ... `ownership test`
    AND NOT "(11)" ... (    f's `incorporated on or after 26 February 2013`
                        AND (    f's `undertakes property development, itself or as a partner`
                             OR  f's `its only activity is holding investments, itself or through a partnership`))
    WHERE
        `ownership test` MEANS
            IF   f's `limited by guarantee`
            THEN "(b)(ii)" ... (f's `all shareholders (or members) individuals throughout the basis period` OR f's `an individual held at least 10% throughout the basis period`)
            ELSE "(b)(i)"  ... (    f's `number of shareholders, directly and beneficially` AT MOST 20
                               AND (f's `all shareholders (or members) individuals throughout the basis period` OR f's `an individual held at least 10% throughout the basis period`))

-- s 43(6C): in any of "the first 3 years of assessment" (s 43(10): the YA of
-- incorporation and the 2 following) falling in or after YA 2008, a
-- qualifying company is taxed under (6D).
@ref s 43(6C), (10) "first 3 years of assessment"
GIVEN f  IS A `Start-up facts`
      ya IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the start-up exemption applies to` f `for YA` ya IF
        `a qualifying company under s 43(10):` f
    AND ya AT LEAST 2008
    AND ya AT LEAST f's `YA of incorporation`
    AND ya AT MOST f's `YA of incorporation` PLUS 2

-- The part of chargeable income that is chargeable with tax.
-- s 43(6B) (YA 2020 onwards, every company or body of persons): "(a) for every
-- dollar of the first $10,000 ..., only 25% is chargeable with tax; and (b) for
-- every dollar of the next $190,000 ..., only 50% is chargeable".
-- s 43(6D)(b) (YA 2020 onwards, a qualifying company in its first 3 YAs): "(i)
-- for every dollar of the first $100,000 ..., only 25% ...; and (ii) for every
-- dollar of the next $100,000 ..., only 50%".
-- (6A), (6D)(a): the earlier tables, for YAs 2008-2019.
@ref s 43(6)-(6D)
GIVEN k            IS A `Kind of person`
      `start-up`   IS A BOOLEAN
      ya           IS A NUMBER
      income       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the chargeable income taxed, after the s 43(6) exemptions, for` k `, start-up:` `start-up` `, YA` ya `, on` income MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (k EQUALS `a company` OR k EQUALS `a body of persons`)
              THEN income
           IF `start-up` AND k EQUALS `a company` AND ya AT LEAST 2020
              THEN `the tax by bands` (LIST (`Band` OF 100000, 25%), (`Band` OF 100000, 50%), (`Band` OF 0, 100%)) `on` income    -- (6D)(b)
           IF `start-up` AND k EQUALS `a company` AND ya AT LEAST 2008
              THEN `the tax by bands` (LIST (`Band` OF 100000, 0), (`Band` OF 200000, 50%), (`Band` OF 0, 100%)) `on` income       -- (6D)(a)
           IF ya AT LEAST 2020
              THEN `the tax by bands` (LIST (`Band` OF 10000, 25%), (`Band` OF 190000, 50%), (`Band` OF 0, 100%)) `on` income      -- (6B)
           IF (k EQUALS `a company` AND ya AT LEAST 2008) OR (k EQUALS `a body of persons` AND ya AT LEAST 2010)
              THEN `the tax by bands` (LIST (`Band` OF 10000, 25%), (`Band` OF 290000, 50%), (`Band` OF 0, 100%)) `on` income      -- (6A)
           OTHERWISE income

§§ `Flat rates on non-residents' gross income (s 43(3)-(5))`

DECLARE `Non-resident gross income` IS ONE OF
    `s 12(6) interest, commission, fee or other payment for a loan or indebtedness`    -- s 43(3)(a): 15%
    `s 12(7)(a) or (b) royalty or payment for the use of movable property`           -- s 43(3A): 10%
    `s 12(7)(d) rent or payment for the use of movable property`                                 -- s 43(3)(b): 15%
    `a REIT distribution to a non-individual without a Singapore PE`                -- s 43(3B): 10%
    `an approved REIT ETF distribution to a non-individual without a Singapore PE`  -- s 43(3C): 10%
    `professional income of a non-resident individual or foreign firm`               -- s 43(4): 15%
    `income as a non-resident arbitrator or mediator`                               -- s 43(4A): 10%

-- s 43(3), (3A), (3B), (3C), (4), (4A): tax on "the gross amount", where the
-- income is not from a trade or business carried on in Singapore and not
-- effectively connected with a permanent establishment here. (3B) and (3C): for
-- distributions made up to 31 December 2030. (4A): for income derived from
-- 1 April 2023 to 31 December 2027. (5): the individual or firm may opt
-- irrevocably for the s 43(1)(b) rate instead.
@ref s 43(3)-(5)
GIVEN i         IS A `Non-resident gross income`
      `payment date` IS A DATE
      `opted for s 43(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the gross-income rate for` i `paid on` `payment date` `, opted:` `opted for s 43(1)(b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `s 12(6) interest, commission, fee or other payment for a loan or indebtedness`  THEN JUST (15%)
    WHEN `s 12(7)(a) or (b) royalty or payment for the use of movable property`         THEN JUST (10%)
    WHEN `s 12(7)(d) rent or payment for the use of movable property`                               THEN JUST (15%)
    WHEN `a REIT distribution to a non-individual without a Singapore PE`               THEN IF `payment date` AT LEAST YMD 2005 2 18 AND `payment date` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31 THEN JUST (10%) ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `an approved REIT ETF distribution to a non-individual without a Singapore PE` THEN IF `payment date` AT LEAST YMD 2018 7 1 AND `payment date` AT MOST YMD 2030 12 31 THEN JUST (10%) ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `professional income of a non-resident individual or foreign firm`              THEN IF `opted for s 43(1)(b)` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (15%)
    WHEN `income as a non-resident arbitrator or mediator`                              THEN
        BRANCH IF `opted for s 43(1)(b)` THEN NOTHING
               IF `payment date` AT LEAST YMD 2023 4 1 AND `payment date` AT MOST YMD 2027 12 31 THEN JUST (10%)
               OTHERWISE JUST (15%)

-- s 43(5): the option must be made "by the 15th day of the second month
-- following the month in which the payment of the income is liable to be made".
@ref s 43(5)
GIVEN `payment liable to be made on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to opt for s 43(1)(b), payment liable on` `payment liable to be made on` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `two months on`) (DATE_MONTH `two months on`) 15
    WHERE
        `two months on` MEANS `add months` (YMD (DATE_YEAR `payment liable to be made on`) (DATE_MONTH `payment liable to be made on`) 1) 2

§§ `Reliefs for non-residents (ss 40A-40D)`

DECLARE `Non-resident relief income` IS ONE OF
    `as a public entertainer`              -- s 40A
    `as a non-resident employee`           -- s 40B
    `from SRS withdrawals`                 -- s 40C

-- ss 40A(2), 40B(2), 40C(2): the rate is reduced to 15% "on every dollar of
-- the chargeable income" where that is the only source, or where total
-- assessable income does not exceed the statutory income from that source;
-- otherwise "on such part of the chargeable income as bears the same proportion
-- to the total chargeable income as the statutory income attributable to [the
-- activity] bears to the total assessable income". s 40A(2A): 10% for a public
-- entertainer's income derived 22 February 2010 to 31 March 2022.
-- ss 40B(3), 40C(3): the relief is "so limited that the tax payable in respect
-- of such income must not be less than that which would be payable by a
-- resident of Singapore in the same circumstances" (with s 39A, (3A)). s 40A
-- has no such limit since Act 41 of 2020 deleted its (3).
-- FORK I2: "the tax ... in respect of such income" is read as the tax on the
-- part of chargeable income the relief reaches; the resident comparison is the
-- caller's figure for that part (`resident tax on that part`). s 40D (two or
-- more of these sources) applies the same rates source by source and is
-- carried as text.
@ref ss 40A(2), (2A), 40B(2)-(3A), 40C(2)-(3A)
GIVEN source                   IS A `Non-resident relief income`
      `chargeable income`      IS A NUMBER
      `statutory income from the source` IS A NUMBER
      `total assessable income` IS A NUMBER
      `the only source in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident tax on that part`   IS A NUMBER
      ya                       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax with the non-resident relief for income` source `, chargeable` `chargeable income` `, from the source` `statutory income from the source` `, assessable` `total assessable income` `, only source:` `the only source in Singapore` `, resident tax` `resident tax on that part` `, YA` ya MEANS
    `relieved tax` PLUS `the rest` TIMES `the non-resident individual rate for YA` ya
    WHERE
        `the part` MEANS
            IF   `the only source in Singapore` OR `total assessable income` AT MOST `statutory income from the source`
            THEN `chargeable income`
            ELSE `chargeable income` TIMES `statutory income from the source` DIVIDED BY `total assessable income`
        `the rest` MEANS `chargeable income` MINUS `the part`
        `at 15%` MEANS `the part` TIMES 15%
        `relieved tax` MEANS
            CONSIDER source
            WHEN `as a public entertainer` THEN `at 15%`
            OTHERWISE IF `at 15%` LESS THAN `resident tax on that part` THEN `resident tax on that part` ELSE `at 15%`

§§ `Rebates and remissions against tax payable`

DECLARE `Order of child` IS ONE OF
    `first child of the family`
    `second child of the family`
    `third child of the family`
    `fourth child of the family`
    `fifth or subsequent child of the family`

-- s 42A(1), (2), (2A), (2B): a resident individual is allowed, for the YA
-- following the birth (or marriage, or adoption), a rebate "against the tax
-- payable" of $5,000 (first child, from 1 January 2008), $10,000 (second, from
-- 1 January 2004), $20,000 (third or fourth, from 1 January 2004), $20,000
-- (fifth or subsequent, from 1 January 2008). (11): the order counts siblings
-- in the same household at the time; the child must be a Singapore citizen
-- then or within 12 months. (10A): none for a child adopted before the
-- individual married.
@ref s 42A(1), (2), (2A), (2B), (10A), (11)
GIVEN order               IS AN `Order of child`
      `the event date`    IS A DATE      -- birth, the parents' marriage, or adoption
      `a citizen then or within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adopted before the claimant married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the parenthood rebate for a` order `, event on` `the event date` `, citizen:` `a citizen then or within 12 months` `, adopted before marriage:` `adopted before the claimant married` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `a citizen then or within 12 months`) OR `adopted before the claimant married`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER order
         WHEN `first child of the family`               THEN IF `the event date` AT LEAST YMD 2008 1 1 THEN 5000 ELSE 0
         WHEN `second child of the family`              THEN IF `the event date` AT LEAST YMD 2004 1 1 THEN 10000 ELSE 0
         WHEN `third child of the family`               THEN IF `the event date` AT LEAST YMD 2004 1 1 THEN 20000 ELSE 0
         WHEN `fourth child of the family`              THEN IF `the event date` AT LEAST YMD 2004 1 1 THEN 20000 ELSE 0
         WHEN `fifth or subsequent child of the family` THEN IF `the event date` AT LEAST YMD 2008 1 1 THEN 20000 ELSE 0

-- s 42A(3): a rebate that cannot be given full effect "by reason of an
-- insufficiency of the tax payable" is carried forward to following YAs.
DECLARE `Rebate applied` HAS
    `tax after rebate`     IS A NUMBER
    `rebate carried forward` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 42A(3)
GIVEN rebate IS A NUMBER
      tax    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rebate applied`
`a rebate of` rebate `against tax of` tax MEANS
    IF   rebate GREATER THAN tax
    THEN `Rebate applied` WITH `tax after rebate` IS 0,              `rebate carried forward` IS rebate MINUS tax
    ELSE `Rebate applied` WITH `tax after rebate` IS tax MINUS rebate, `rebate carried forward` IS 0

DECLARE `Company remission` HAS
    `tax remitted`  IS A NUMBER
    `cash grant`    IS A NUMBER

-- ss 92J (YA 2024) and 92L (YA 2025): remission of "the lower of — (a) 50% of
-- the tax payable for that year of assessment (excluding any tax levied under
-- section 43(3), (3A), (3B) and (3C)), less the cash grant of $2,000 made to
-- the company under subsection (3), where applicable; (b) $40,000, less the cash
-- grant of $2,000 ..., where applicable." (2): "where 50% of the tax payable
-- under subsection (1)(a) is less than the cash grant of $2,000, the amount in
-- subsection (1)(a) is nil." (3): the $2,000 grant if the company made a CPF
-- contribution for at least one local employee in the preceding calendar year.
-- s 92L(4): no grant (unless permitted) if, at disbursement, the company is not
-- carrying on a trade or business, is in liquidation or receivership, or has
-- ceased to exist.
@ref ss 92J, 92L
GIVEN ya                     IS A NUMBER
      `tax payable, excluding s 43(3)-(3C)` IS A NUMBER
      `CPF for a local employee in the preceding calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 92L(4) bar at disbursement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Company remission`
`the company remission for YA` ya `on tax of` `tax payable, excluding s 43(3)-(3C)` `, local CPF:` `CPF for a local employee in the preceding calendar year` `, barred:` `a s 92L(4) bar at disbursement` MEANS
    IF   NOT (ya EQUALS 2024 OR ya EQUALS 2025)
    THEN `Company remission` WITH `tax remitted` IS 0, `cash grant` IS 0
    ELSE `Company remission` WITH `tax remitted` IS `remitted`, `cash grant` IS `grant`
    WHERE
        `grant` MEANS
            IF   `CPF for a local employee in the preceding calendar year` AND NOT (ya EQUALS 2025 AND `a s 92L(4) bar at disbursement`)
            THEN 2000
            ELSE 0
        `half` MEANS `tax payable, excluding s 43(3)-(3C)` TIMES 50%
        `(a)` MEANS IF `half` LESS THAN `grant` THEN 0 ELSE `half` MINUS `grant`
        `(b)` MEANS 40000 MINUS `grant`
        `remitted` MEANS IF `(a)` LESS THAN `(b)` THEN `(a)` ELSE `(b)`
